# Build artifacts
node_modules/
# ...including when it is a symlink, which the trailing-slash form above misses.
# packages/ui/node_modules is a link to frontend/node_modules so the kit can be
# built offline before a root `npm install` has hoisted the workspace deps.
node_modules
.venv/
backend/.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
dist/
dist-springer/
build/
.next/
.cache/
.vite/

# Mobile / Expo
mobile/.expo/
mobile/node_modules/

# Runtime state — local cache + ephemeral runs, never source
.runtime/
*.log
cron_agent.log
/tmp/

# Secrets — defense in depth (also handled by symlink layout)
*.env
secrets.env
auth.env

# Generated
status.md
.runtime/finance-cache.json

# BirdNET: local-preview copy of the sanitized dataset + any local fixture DB
apps/birds/public-site/birds-public.json
apps/birds/**/*.db

# Infra deploy state (containers, secrets dropped in by deploy scripts)
infra/open-wearables/repo/

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Build artifacts / tooling caches (not source)
*.tsbuildinfo
.playwright-mcp/

# Map basemap — large regenerable data file (go-pmtiles extract), not source.
# Regenerate with `pmtiles extract` (see docs/app-platform-plan.md).
*.pmtiles
frontend/public/basemap/

# Local marketplace release artifacts — git bundles can be large and are
# regenerable from the source projects; the catalog (registry.json) IS tracked.
registry-bundles/

# Per-project working trees, build-agent scratch dirs, and worktrees.
# Each is its own git repo / ephemeral working state — not Workshop source.
# Only scaffold templates are tracked.
/projects/*
!/projects/_templates/
/build-agents/
/branches/

# Per-instance state — NEVER tracked. Workshop is a container: which apps are
# installed, the project/build-agent registries, the app identity manifests, and
# the operator's commute data are all instance state that lives in .runtime/ (or,
# for these legacy locations, is gitignored here) so a fresh clone starts blank
# and inherits no operator's apps or data. See docs/apps-are-pluggable.md.
/projects.json
/build_agents.json
/backend/apps.json
# Runtime-minted resource capability tokens (Store grants). Instance state, not
# config; the app-level grants.json seed stays tracked, this does not.
/backend/resource-grants.json
/commute/schedule.json
# User-scope agent definition INSTANCES (declarative registry of record, but they
# hold the operator's personas/config) are instance state. Project-scoped agent
# defs live under /projects/* and are already ignored above.
#
# `/agents/*` ignores the CONTENTS rather than the directory, because git cannot
# re-include anything under an excluded directory — the same shape `/projects/*`
# + `!/projects/_templates/` uses. The shipped agent TEMPLATES are source (they
# are forked into instances, never run in place), so they are tracked.
/agents/*
!/agents/_templates/
# The built-in app assistants' definitions (budget, finance, commute, location).
# Shipped source, not instance state: they define personas that come WITH the
# app, so they are tracked for the same reason the templates are. Also outside
# the roster's non-recursive `agents/*.md` glob, so nothing here is dispatched.
!/agents/apps/
/commute/legs.json
/commute/targets.json
/commute/sources/registry.json
/commute/notes/

# Ephemeral working files — NEVER committed. Put smoke tests, scratch scripts,
# throwaway probes, and ad-hoc working notes in one of these folders (anywhere in
# the tree) instead of dropping stray test_*/tmp_* files into source dirs.
scratch/
tmp/
**/scratch/
**/tmp/
.tasks.json.lock

# Per-rig engineering records for an installed app: one operator's hardware,
# tailnet addresses and bring-up history. Useful on the box, never in the repo.
apps/birds/BIRDSTATION-CONTEXT*.md

# Operator state, not platform source: declared Store access rules and the
# append-only routing-decision log. Templates: backend/store-policies.example.json.
backend/store-policies.json
shared/relay-corpus.jsonl

# The work queue is instance state. A fresh clone starts empty, the way it
# starts with no projects and no installed apps.
#
# `shared/queue/.tasks.json` was tracked until the ADR 0019 stage 2 cutover
# (2026-08-16). Tickets for the relational scopes live in Postgres now and that
# file stopped being written, so a tracked copy could only go stale in the diff
# of every future commit. The file itself stays on disk as the cutover backup;
# this untracks it rather than deleting it.
#
# DELIBERATELY UNANCHORED, since 2026-08-27. These were `/.tasks.json` and
# `/TODO.md`, matching only at the repo root -- so a worker's ticket directory
# anywhere else was fair game for `git add`, and one was committed: the
# hex-named `4a79ffc515844ca2a48a369b7ca7b0a7/` (379d82fa) carried a live
# ticket queue in the repo for anyone who cloned it. Four more such directories
# are on disk right now. A work queue is instance state at ANY depth, so the
# pattern matches at any depth, and the tracked exceptions are named below
# rather than relied on to be the only ones the anchor happened to spare.
.tasks.json
TODO.md
# The scaffold templates ship a TODO.md as scaffold CONTENT (it is what a new
# project starts from), and shared/queue/TODO.md is the tracked human-readable
# queue. Both are source, so both are re-included. Their sibling .tasks.json is
# not: that is the machine state.
!/projects/_templates/**/TODO.md
!/shared/queue/TODO.md

# Tenant operational records: bring-up playbook and security audits of one
# operator's own box. Kept on disk, not shipped as platform documentation.
docs/masini/

# ---- ONE OPERATOR'S APPS ARE NOT PLATFORM SOURCE -------------------------
# 2026-08-20. An app is installed content; the platform is the container. A
# clone by anyone else must contain no trace of whoever ran the instance it was
# cloned from, and until now it contained 143 tracked files of one.
#
# These four are the part that could be untracked immediately, because nothing
# in the build imports them: every reference is a runtime path lookup over an
# env-overridable directory, or a comment. The files stay on disk and keep
# working here; they just stop being in the repo.
#
# The REST of an app (its React pages under frontend/src/pages/apps, its
# route/service modules in the flat backend dirs) cannot follow yet: the
# frontend registry statically imports those pages, so gitignoring them would
# break a fresh clone's build. That needs the app loader and the AppSpec seams.
# Plan: docs/platform-redesign/app-separation-and-github-2026-08-20.md.
#
# History is untouched: `git log --follow` still has all of it.
# Anchored with a leading slash, all four. A bare `commute/` matches ANY
# directory of that name at any depth, which silently swallowed
# `backend/services/commute/` -- still-tracked platform-side app code, so
# nothing broke, but the next file added there would have been ignored without a
# word. Same trap for `apps/` (frontend/src/pages/apps/) and `agents/apps/`.
/apps/
/agents/apps/
/backend/mcp/plaid/
/commute/

# COMPACTION HANDOFFS ARE INSTANCE STATE, NOT SOURCE.
# `shared/knowledge/<scope>/working-state.md` is written by the summariser every
# time a chat in that scope compacts, and overwritten by the next one. Two
# consequences made tracking them actively harmful:
#   * The tree was never clean. done.sh saw an uncommitted file it could not
#     attribute, so it fell back to scoped checks and the full reviewer.sh had
#     not run all session.
#   * They carry this installation's identity. The summariser writes whatever
#     the chat discussed, and on 2026-09-01 that was the operator's own domain,
#     twice, which check_no_hardcoding correctly counts as a new identity
#     reference in tracked source.
# They stay on disk and keep working; a new chat still reads its scope's file.
shared/knowledge/**/working-state.md
